# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  .env.example  —  copy this file to  .env  and fill in your real values.
#  The real .env is GITIGNORED, so your secrets are never committed/pushed.
#  On a real web host, set these as environment variables instead of using .env.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Turn on inquiry emails (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Every inquiry is ALWAYS saved in the admin. Fill these in to ALSO get them by email.
# 1) The Gmail account that SENDS the mail (usually your business Gmail):
SHREYA_MAIL_USERNAME=shreyaauto.enterprises@gmail.com
# 2) A Gmail *App Password* (16 characters) — NOT your normal password.
#    Create it at: Google Account → Security → 2-Step Verification → App passwords.
#    (2-Step Verification must be ON first.) Paste it here with no spaces:
SHREYA_MAIL_PASSWORD=your16charapppassword
# 3) Where inquiry emails are delivered (can be the same Gmail, or any inbox):
SHREYA_MAIL_TO=shreyaauto.enterprises@gmail.com

# ── Other secrets (mainly for production; local dev is fine without them) ─────
# SHREYA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=choose-a-strong-password
# SHREYA_SECRET_KEY=paste-a-long-random-hex-string
# SHREYA_ADMIN_PATH=office-2f9k7x
